        ecrm:P3_has_note    "This floral-patterned silk velvet was produced in Isfahan as dress fabric. When Shah Abbas I made the city his capital shortly before 1600, he developed it as a centre of luxury textile production. Silk velvets were made there in abundance, both for local use and for export. Many had floral patterns. Some were composed of fantastic blossoms, others (like this piece) of flowers closer to nature."@en ;
